269
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:48,420
Yeah, hi, hi.

270
00:13:50,210 --> 00:13:51,400
How's it going?

271
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:53,490
Uh, can't complain.

272
00:13:53,490 --> 00:13:54,890
Thanks for asking.

273
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:59,890
Well, what were you doing out at 3:00 in the morning?

274
00:14:00,190 --> 00:14:03,490
Well, uh, uh... what are you doing up?

275
00:14:04,430 --> 00:14:06,230
I was using the bathroom.

276
00:14:06,830 --> 00:14:09,360
Yeah, well, so was I.

277
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:11,570
Really?

278
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:14,180
I didn't see you in there.

279
00:14:17,250 --> 00:14:20,710
Obviously... when I saw that you were in ours,

280
00:14:20,710 --> 00:14:23,590
I went and used another one.

281
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:26,740
Where?

282
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:31,080
The, the gas station across the street.

283
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,080
In your pajamas?

284
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:34,980
Yes.

285
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:38,430
Without shoes?

286
00:14:40,030 --> 00:14:40,980
Yes.

287
00:14:43,070 --> 00:14:44,740
On a cold winter's night?

288
00:14:47,610 --> 00:14:48,670
Yes.

289
00:14:52,890 --> 00:14:54,740
Seems unlikely.

290
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:57,000
Did you bring your asthma inhaler?

291
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,580
Uh, uh, uh, yes, I did.

292
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:05,780
Well, then, I guess it's plausible.

293
00:15:07,370 --> 00:15:09,690
- D-- hang on a second, mister. - What?

294
00:15:11,350 --> 00:15:14,550
After you used the facilities at the gas station,

295
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:17,090
- did you make a purchase? - What?

296
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:20,560
It's customary, when using the restroom

297
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:24,040
at a retail establishment, to make a small purchase.

298
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:24,940
Did you?

299
00:15:25,850 --> 00:15:26,760
No.

300
00:15:28,210 --> 00:15:29,720
Here's two dollars.

301
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:35,060
Go buy some beef jerky.

302
00:15:42,470 --> 00:15:44,300
I don't want beef jerky.

303
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:49,470
It's not about you.

304
00:15:49,470 --> 00:15:52,140
It's about a poor immigrant from Pakistan

305
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:53,780
trying to make his way in America

306
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:55,310
by working the graveyard shift

307
00:15:55,310 --> 00:15:57,300
at the Colorado Boulevard Chevron.

308
00:16:00,810 --> 00:16:01,960
Fine.

309
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:06,870
Needy Baby, Greedy Baby indeed.

310
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:11,000
Leonard will be here in a moment.

311
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,450
He's looking for a different parking space.

312
00:16:13,450 --> 00:16:14,400
Why?

313
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:15,950
We were next to a car

314
00:16:15,950 --> 00:16:18,700
with an "Ask me about my grandchildren." bumper sticker,

315
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:21,070
and I was afraid if we ran into them on the way out,

316
00:16:21,070 --> 00:16:23,170
I'd be obligated to do so.

317
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:28,350
I'm so disappointed it didn't work with him and Penny.

318
00:16:28,350 --> 00:16:29,880
Me, too.

319
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,120
Out of deference to them,

320
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:33,820
let's not flaunt our happy relationship.

321
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:37,100
You have a keen insight into the human heart,

322
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:38,610
Amy Farrah Fowler.

323
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:44,750
We are next to a Suburu with a Gore/Lieberman bumper sticker.

324
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:47,500
Well, I doubt they'd want to talk about that, so we're fine.

325
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:50,820
I'm surprised to see you here

326
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:52,930
after it went so badly with Penny.

327
00:16:52,930 --> 00:16:54,640
Well, hey, we're grown-ups.

328
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:56,200
We can still be friends.

329
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:58,390
Boy, I don't know if I could be friends with Howie

330
00:16:58,400 --> 00:16:59,800
if we broke up.

331
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:00,650
Why not?

332
00:17:00,650 --> 00:17:02,980
I'm a very vengeful person.

333
00:17:04,970 --> 00:17:05,960
Really?

334
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:08,530
With access to weaponized smallpox.

335
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:12,990
Here you go, guys, let me get you going with some water.

336
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:14,610
You need menus or you know what you want?

337
00:17:14,610 --> 00:17:15,550
Leonard knows what he wants,

338
00:17:15,550 --> 00:17:17,690
but it looks like he's not gonna get it from you.

339
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:20,180
Howard.

340
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:21,930
No, that's okay, Bernadette.

341
00:17:21,930 --> 00:17:24,230
Sometimes these things just don't work out.

342
00:17:24,230 --> 00:17:25,670
Yeah, it's all good.

343
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:28,560
We-We'll always have feelings for each other.

344
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:33,030
Oh, that's nice.

345
00:17:33,770 --> 00:17:35,830
See, she knew what "always" meant.

346
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:39,110
Wow, you're like a dog with a bone, aren't you?

347
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,280
I'm just making a point.

348
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:43,520
Is the point that you don't know when to let something go?

349
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,660
People, people,

350
00:17:44,660 --> 00:17:47,560
please, before you say something you both regret,

351
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:49,350
I'd like to place my order.

352
00:17:51,220 --> 00:17:52,300
Yeah, just hang on, Sheldon.

353
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:53,690
You know why we can't be together?

354
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:55,220
Because you always have to be right.

355
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:56,770
Oh, that is not true.

356
00:17:56,770 --> 00:17:58,040
I got to go with Leonard on this.

357
00:17:58,040 --> 00:18:00,290
He is wrong more than anyone I know.

358
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:03,210
You know what? I just realized I'm on a break.

359
00:18:03,210 --> 00:18:04,880
I'll get someone else.

360
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:09,000
Leonard, promise me that when our new waitress comes over,

361
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,900
you will not start a complicated on-again,

362
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:12,370
off-again relationship with her,

363
00:18:12,370 --> 00:18:14,270
because I am very, very hungry.

364
00:18:26,830 --> 00:18:28,380
Unbelievable.

365
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:34,140
Mind explaining to me why you were being

366
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:35,560
such a jerk at the restaurant?

367
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:37,630
I was trying to act like we weren't seeing each other.

368
00:18:37,630 --> 00:18:38,900
- That was the plan, right?  - No,

369
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:41,310
the plan was to tell people we decided to stay friends.

370
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,480
That's a little hard to do

371
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:45,400
when you're always being such a tool bag.

372
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:48,840
You know what? I don't have to stand here and take this crap.

373
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,430
The hell do you think you're going?

374
00:18:50,430 --> 00:18:53,550
Isn't sex after fighting kind of what we do now?!

375
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:56,680
Yeah, kind of, yeah.

376
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,300
What are we doing?

377
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:07,600
What do you mean?

378
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:11,800
Every scenario I play out for you and me ends badly.

379
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:13,800
That's because you overthink everything.

380
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:15,970
Leonard, are you listening to me?

381
00:19:15,990 --> 00:19:17,520
What? Yeah.

382
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:19,450
This is a disaster.

383
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:20,720
I distinctly ordered

384
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:23,640
the Leonard Nimoy Mr. Spock cardboard standee.

385
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:25,120
Why would I feel safer

386
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:27,410
with Zachary Quinto at the foot of my bed?

387
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:32,750
I don't know, he was pretty badass on Heroes.

388
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:36,000
You're right, I'll give him a shot.

389
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:39,670
Hang on.

390
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:41,720
Penny, do you have plans for dinner?

391
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,130
Why, you guys going somewhere?

392
00:19:43,130 --> 00:19:44,570
No, I mean just you and me.

393
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,740
Uh, have you thought this through?

394
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:54,290
Yes, and I think we should go anyway.

395
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:57,920
No, can't do it.

396
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,600
Sorry, Quinto, you're going back.

397
00:20:06,590 --> 00:20:08,360
If you and Leonard get back together,

398
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:09,980
Sheldon and I will finally have someone

399
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:11,500
to go on double dates with.

400
00:20:11,670 --> 00:20:13,280
What about me and Howard?

401
00:20:13,850 --> 00:20:15,790
Fine, we can double with you, too.

402
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:18,230
So insecure.

403
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,690
Where are you guys going to eat?

404
00:20:22,980 --> 00:20:24,500
Penny?

405
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:30,880
Do you, Penny, take Leonard to be your lawful wedded husband?

406
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:39,780
Well, it's a little late for me

407
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,900
to start saying no, isn't it?

408
00:20:44,050 --> 00:20:45,140
Penny.

409
00:20:45,790 --> 00:20:49,650
Sorry, just remembered I've got to stop at the drugstore.

